                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Play Time: 41 hours\nAchievements: 15 of 15. 100%\nDate/Version: September 9th 2026\nRating: 7 out of 10\n\n\n“Alvora Tactics is an indie Tactics RPG that combines strategic combat with immersive exploration. Explore and conquer Great Serpent Alvora with your own customizable band of warriors!”\n\nI'm not sure how to review this so let's get it started.\nI spent roughly 9 hours if not more trying to get 1 achievement.\nI enjoyed myself it's been a while since I played any tactics game of this sort.\nThe music was good, the story wasn't amazing but it was a story. Apparently it's set in a world that the designers created in the past. I could be wrong about that but in any case this game was interesting. Little puzzles, here and there, you can interact with the environment and manipulate the battlefield. Some classes help you with the puzzles, getting additional items, etc. Money in the beginning was super super tight. But within time you kind of find some goods, and looping is helpful. Each boss had it's on play style which was fun, and (spoilers) the game may have more at the end.\nOverall this was an enjoyable game.\nFor the price and if it's on sale it was completely worth it. \n\n\n“Combine 10 races, 23 classes, 150+ upgrade-able abilities, and 50+ passives to create your ideal party\nUnique fantasy setting; no elves, orcs, or dwarves”",
